57,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'derives the intended local hop sequence from the ticket's core STATUS event log ... anchors on Jira's current status, and re-attempts each intermediate hop ... aborting to drift on the first hop the target rejects'","Retrieved prior art (Exalate holiday-integration recipe; DefectDojo Jira guide; Atlassian advanced-workflow-configuration; Stack Overflow 'listing all Jira transitions via API') shows the common industry approach is target-workflow transition mapping / path resolution against the destination's allowed transitions, not replaying the source's historical hops","ABSENCE: the plan does not cite or contrast any prior-art approach for the one novel algorithm it adds; it justifies replay only against rebar's own primitives"],"finding":"S6's transition-replay algorithm (novel: replay the SOURCE ticket's recorded hop sequence) is introduced without weighing it against the established alternative of resolving a transition PATH against the TARGET workflow's own allowed-transition graph, which is how Jira workflows and mainstream sync tools reach an intended status.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd8a5277d503e3c2d","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / S6 — Transition replay; AC line 'A non-allowed transition is attempted by replay of rebar's recorded hops'","norm_id":"n2d388bff35e22092","priority":0.0943,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Target project's workflow permits a direct or shorter path to the intended status, but the source's recorded hop sequence does not align with the target's allowed transitions, so replay aborts to drift where a target-graph path solve would have succeeded","A target status reachable only via a transition the source never recorded (target-specific intermediate) is never reached under recorded-hop replay"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a short prior-art note to S6 acknowledging target-workflow path-resolution (used by Jira workflows and tools like Exalate) and state the explicit reason recorded-hop replay is chosen instead — e.g. it stays provider-neutral and avoids inventing hops the operator never authored — while noting the accepted cost (more drift when the source trail doesn't match the target graph).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an S6 (d458) acceptance criterion asserting that a ticket with no surviving recorded STATUS trail (e.g. a compacted ticket) degrades the failed transition to drift/pre-S6 backstop without inventing hops.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8125,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent AC: 'A non-allowed transition is attempted by replay of rebar's recorded hops and, failing that (or when no recorded trail survives, e.g. a compacted ticket), drifts'","Parent Approach: 'When no recorded trail survives — e.g. a compacted ticket whose STATUS events are folded into a snapshot that keeps only the final status — replay is not applicable and the failed transition 